From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:04:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: put the C heap in a named dynamic area

UnixLib puts the heap in a dynamic area when __dynamic_da_name is defined
(otherwise it has to fit in the WimpSlot, or needs a <prog>$Heap
variable). "Warzone2100 Heap", up to 512MB, removed when the game quits.
---
 src/main.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index 0c6e138..07fac08 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -513,6 +513,15 @@ static void initialize_ConfigDir(void)
 }
 
 
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+/* Put the C heap in a dynamic area with a fixed name (as the RISC OS port of
+ * OpenTTD does). UnixLib otherwise looks for a "<program>$Heap" variable
+ * named after the command line; without a dynamic area the heap has to fit
+ * in the WimpSlot. The area is removed when the game quits. */
+const char * const __dynamic_da_name = "Warzone2100 Heap";
+int __dynamic_da_max_size = 512 * 1024 * 1024;
+#endif
+
 /*!
  * Initialize the PhysicsFS library.
  */
